Here’s a full working solution for integrating drag-and-drop variable tags into your Quill editor using a custom blot.


---

✅ Step 1: Create VariableTagBlot.js

// src/components/QuillBlots/VariableTagBlot.js
import Quill from 'quill';

const Inline = Quill.import('blots/inline');

class VariableTagBlot extends Inline {
  static create(value) {
    const node = super.create();
    node.setAttribute('data-name', value);
    node.setAttribute('contenteditable', 'false');
    node.classList.add('variable-tag');
    node.innerText = `{{${value}}}`;
    return node;
  }

  static value(node) {
    return node.getAttribute('data-name');
  }
}

VariableTagBlot.blotName = 'variableTag';
VariableTagBlot.tagName = 'span';
VariableTagBlot.className = 'variable-tag';

export default VariableTagBlot;


---

✅ Step 2: Register the blot in your main component

At the top of your EmailTemplate component file, add:

import VariableTagBlot from './QuillBlots/VariableTagBlot'; // Adjust the path as needed
Quill.register({ 'formats/variableTag': VariableTagBlot });


---

✅ Step 3: Style your variable tags

Create or update your quill.css:

.variable-tag {
  background-color: #1976d2;
  color: white;
  padding: 3px 6px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  margin: 0 2px;
  display: inline-block;
  font-weight: 600;
  font-family: monospace;
  pointer-events: none; /* Prevent user interaction */
}


---

✅ Step 4: Update handleDrop in EmailTemplate.js

Replace your current handleDrop method with:

const handleDrop = (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  if (!isEditing) return;

  const editor = bodyEditorRef.current?.getEditor();
  if (!editor) return;

  const tag = e.dataTransfer.getData("text").replace(/[{}]/g, ""); // "DATE", etc.
  const range = editor.getSelection(true);

  if (range) {
    editor.insertEmbed(range.index, 'variableTag', tag, 'user');
    editor.setSelection(range.index + 1); // Move cursor after inserted tag
  }
};


---

✅ Step 5: Drag Source (already correct in your code)

No change needed to this:

{draftVar.map((label) => (
  <span
    key={label}
    draggable={isEditing}
    onDragStart={handleDragStart}
    ...
  >
    {label}
  </span>
))}


---

✅ Final Result

Dragging {{DATE}} into the editor results in:

<span class="variable-tag" data-name="DATE" contenteditable="false">{{DATE}}</span>

This appears as a styled, non-editable token. Quill preserves these as inline spans and includes them in content export.


